# Frontend.
#
# Only public values belong here. Everything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into code every visitor
# downloads, so a credential placed here is a published credential. `npm run test` reads the built
# bundle and fails if a backend variable name or a connection string appears in it.

# Where the API answers.
#
# Unset, or a relative path, means the API shares this origin and a gateway proxies /api to it.
# An absolute origin means the API is deployed as its own host, which is this platform's shape:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.websitebuilder.oneplataforma.com/api/v1
#
# The session cookie still travels, because the application and the API share a registrable domain
# and the cookie is host-only to the API. It is never sent to a published customer site.
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1
